**VERDICT: The census and decomposition are exact (21 live exits in `dev_sgi_re.c`; 13 in `sgi_re` decomposing into 6 width kills, 6 read kills, 1 unmapped fallback). All 6 read kills are 100% reachable via guest loads on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`. The scope split between #497 (width kills) and `sgirekills` (read kills) is correct. All 6 read arms qualify for ACCEPT because backing state exists in `struct sgi_re_data`. One malloc serves all four handlers, confirming shared latch reachability. The exclusion of `sgi_de` width kill from #497 is confirmed.**

