### Q1 — Reachability and Address Windows

**Reachability:** **ALL SIX read kills are fully reachable** by an ordinary guest 64-bit load instruction (`ld`) on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`.
- Base registration: [`src/machines/machine_sgi.c:500`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/machines/machine_sgi.c#L500) passes base `0x15000000` to [`dev_sgi_re_init`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L385).
- In [`dev_sgi_re_init`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L392), `sgi_re` is registered at `baseaddr + 0x1000` (`0x15001000`) with length `DEV_SGI_RE_LENGTH = 0x1000` ([`src/include/devices.h:403`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/devices.h#L403)), covering physical range `0x15001000`–`0x15001fff`.
- At [`dev_sgi_re.c:228`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L228), `relative_addr += 0x1000;` restores the full offset relative to `0x15000000`.
- All 6 windows lie completely within `0x15001000`–`0x150017ff`, well inside the registered `0x1000` window. None is shadowed, and the `else if` cascade is strictly disjoint.

#### Address Derivation Table for the Six Windows

| Window Name | Header Macro ([`crmfbreg.h`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/crmfbreg.h#L230-L237)) | Dispatched `relative_addr` Range | Guest Physical Address (GPA) | Guest Virtual Address (GVA in KSEG1, 32-bit) | 64-bit Direct Uncached GVA (XKPHYS) | Read Kill Site |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `CRIME_RE_TLB_A` | `CRIME_RE_TLB_A` (`0x1000`) | `0x1000`–`0x11ff` (512 B) | `0x15001000`–`0x150011ff` | `0xb5001000`–`0xb50011ff` | `0x9000000015001000` | [`dev_sgi_re.c:245`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L245) |
