### Q3 — What Should a Read Return?

**Member Applying:** **ACCEPT** applies to all six read arms.

**Struct Evidence ([`dev_sgi_re.c:58-67`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L58-L67)):**
The struct [`struct sgi_re_data`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L58) already stores all data written by the guest:
1. `CRIME_RE_TLB_A`: `re_tlb_a[256]` written at [lines 238–242](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L238-L242). Read returns 4 halfwords (`tlbi..tlbi+3`) packed into `odata`.
2. `CRIME_RE_TLB_B`: `re_tlb_b[256]` written at [lines 255–259](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L255-L259). Read returns 4 halfwords (`tlbi..tlbi+3`) packed into `odata`.
3. `CRIME_RE_TLB_C`: `re_tlb_c[256]` written at [lines 272–276](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L272-L276). Read returns 4 halfwords (`tlbi..tlbi+3`) packed into `odata`.
4. `CRIME_RE_TEX`: `re_tex[112]` written at [lines 289–293](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L289-L293). Backing array `re_tex[112]` exists in the struct to serve readback.
5. `CRIME_RE_LINEAR_A`: `re_linear_a[32]` written at [lines 340–341](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L340-L341). Read returns `((uint64_t)d->re_linear_a[tlbi] << 32ULL) | d->re_linear_a[tlbi+1]`.
6. `CRIME_RE_LINEAR_B`: `re_linear_b[32]` written at [lines 356–357](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L356-L357). Read returns `((uint64_t)d->re_linear_b[tlbi] << 32ULL) | d->re_linear_b[tlbi+1]`.

Furthermore, [`DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_re)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L221) already has `uint64_t odata = 0;` declared at [line 224](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L224) and [`memory_writemax64(cpu, data, len, odata)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L376) at line 376. Setting `odata` in the read arm automatically accepts and returns the stored data to the guest.

