### Q4 — The House Idiom and Shared Allocation

**Confirmation:** **CONFIRMED**.

1. **Shared Malloc**:
   In [`dev_sgi_re_init`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L385-L398):
   - [Line 389](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L389): `CHECK_ALLOCATION(d = (struct sgi_re_data *) malloc(sizeof(struct sgi_re_data)));`
   - [Line 390](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L390): `memset(d, 0, sizeof(struct sgi_re_data));`
   - [Line 392](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L392): registers `dev_sgi_re_access` with cookie `d`.
   - [Line 395](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L395): calls `dev_sgi_de_init(mem, baseaddr + 0x2000, d);` which registers `dev_sgi_de_access` with `d` ([line 925](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L925)).
   - [Line 396](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L396): calls `dev_sgi_mte_init(mem, baseaddr + 0x3000, d);` which registers `dev_sgi_mte_access` with `d` ([line 1279](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L1279)).
   - [Line 397](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L397): calls `dev_sgi_de_status_init(mem, baseaddr + 0x4000, d);` which registers `dev_sgi_de_status_access` with `d` ([line 1338](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L1338)).
2. **Latch Infrastructure**:
   Any latch field placed in [`struct sgi_re_data`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L58-L73) is zero-initialized by `memset` and instantly accessible to all four device handlers.

