### Q5 — The Seventh Site (`DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_de)`)

**Confirmation of Exclusion:** **CONFIRMED**.

**Detailed Analysis:**
1. **Different Handler & Registration**:
   - `sgi_de` is registered at `0x15002000` ([`dev_sgi_re.c:395, 925`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L395)), distinct from `sgi_re` at `0x15001000`.
2. **Different Accept Set**:
   - `sgi_re` accept set is strictly `{8}` ([`dev_sgi_re.c:231`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L231)).
   - `sgi_de` accept set is `{4, 8}` ([`dev_sgi_re.c:680, 687`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L680-L695)); host kill at [line 694](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L694) triggers for `len in {1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7}`.
3. **`sgi_de` Genuinely Serves Reads**:
   - Unlike `sgi_re`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_de)` **does not suffer from missing read arms**.
   - For all handled registers at `len == 4` ([line 691](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L691)) and `len == 8` ([line 685](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L685)), reads directly load `d->de_reg[regnr]` into `odata` and write it to guest memory at [line 914](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L914).
   - Its unhandled default at [line 900–908](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c#L900-L908) prints `fatal(...)` but does **not** call `exit(1)`.
   - Therefore, keeping `sgi_de` width handling in `sgidewidth` as an independent round is verified and correct.
